::recipe
conversion stage: initial

name: Fresh Guacamole
source: https://publicdomainrecipes.com/guacamole/
source author: yaroslav-smirnov
source license: Public domain (Unlicense)
ingredients: mixed
category: dip
tags: avocado, fresh, Mexican-inspired
dietary: vegan
serves: ~2
image: guacamole.webp

::ingredients

(avocado, Hass) 2
(onion, medium) 1/4
(tomato, small) 1
(cilantro) as needed
(lime) 1
(salt) to taste
(black pepper) to taste
(totopos, for serving) as desired

::equipment

(bowl)

::instructions

(avocado) <halve>
    <remove pulp, bowl>
    <mash>
    + (lime: juice)
    <mix>
    <mash, some more>

(cilantro) <mince>
(tomato) <mince>
(onion) <mince>

{guacamole} =
    (avocado) +
    (cilantro) +
    (tomato) +
    (onion) +
    (salt) +
    (black pepper)

{guacamole} <mix, thoroughly>
    <serve, fresh, with totopos>

::notes
The source recommends eating the guacamole fresh because avocado oxidises quickly and can
lose colour and texture within a few hours.